<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see sun except rain in centre.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see sun except rain in centre.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Monday were forecast to see sun except for some thundershowers in the central region, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see mainly sunny skies with highs of 15 to 24 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see cloudy skies, a few thundershowers and highs of 18 to 28 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see sunny skies with highs of 16 to 25 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
